/// in every style of [rowStyles] whose condition holds for it, beside being selected.
///
/// A column carrying an inline filter draws its control under its heading, read off
/// the enclosing [CruftFreeFilterBar]; the last heading then holds the one "Clear filters"
/// control (and, for a `filtersHidden` table, the control showing and hiding the
/// filters), and the table stays shown while its filters match nothing, so the reader
/// keeps typing in them. A table holding every row of its source sorts them itself:
/// [clientSort] is its sort and [onClientSort] receives a pressed header's column.
///
/// A table with a [rowDetail] leads the first cell of each row the detail [CruftFreeRowDetail.offers]
/// with a disclosure control, and draws an open row's detail in a row beneath it.
class CruftFreeTable<T> extends StatelessWidget {
